%%HP: T(0)A(D)F(.);
@
@ REST  (Full Scanner Memory Bank Restore)
@ Arguments: None
@
@ This script will restore all the frequency banks stored in the HP48
@ into the scanner.  This is a slow process and will take several minutes.
@ Also, this will wipe out whatever is currently in the scanner memory
@ without any further prompt. This assumes that all valid frequency bank files
@ are present, namely: BNK0, BNK1, ... ,BNK8 and BNK9.
@
@ Author: Pepin Torres, P.E. - Waltham, Massachusetts, USA
@ E-mail: pepin [dot] torres {at} g m a i l (dot) com
@ Version: 1.0
@ Date: 02/21/2009
@ Created using HPUserEdit 5 [http://www.gaak.org/hpuser]

"RESTORE ALL BANKS?"
{ {"Yes, restore."   1} , { "No, quit now"   0}} 2
CHOOSE DROP
IF 1 == THEN
  BNK0 SCNR
  BNK1 SCNR
  BNK2 SCNR
  BNK3 SCNR
  BNK4 SCNR
  BNK5 SCNR
  BNK6 SCNR
  BNK7 SCNR
  BNK8 SCNR
  BNK9 SCNR
  "Scanner memory was restored" MSGBOX
ELSE
  "Scanner restore CANCELED" MSGBOX
END
 